    "narrative": "For August 25, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (75.05) and **Lawrence Butler** (70.87) represent our strongest offensive engine. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** commands the slate with an elite 75.05 score, bolstered by a prime #2 hole opportunity against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, whose 4.42 xERA offers significant upside. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a strong +13% dynamic platoon edge against Taj Bradley; despite Bradley\u2019s respectable peripherals, the combination of a favorable hitter's park and **Lawrence Butler**\u2019s recent surge makes him a core anchor today. We are also capitalizing on **Jonathan Aranda** (65.40), whose +12% platoon adjustment against Jackson Jobe makes him a sneaky value play in the 5-hole.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final bench spot, where **Justin Crawford** (50.50) narrowly missed the cut behind **Tyler Freeman** (53.55). While **Justin Crawford** offers elite speed\u2014a priority given our scarcity concerns\u2014the optimizer favored **Tyler Freeman** due to a slightly more favorable matchup profile, despite **Tyler Freeman** battling a -6% order penalty in the 8-hole. Risks remain elevated today as every rostered player is currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status; we must be particularly wary of **Cal Raleigh** (48.96) and **Gleyber Torres** (52.38). **Gleyber Torres** faces a tough +10% order boost despite a poor SP matchup against Ian Seymour, and any late-breaking news regarding his status or weather could force a rapid pivot to **Dylan Beavers** or **JJ Bleday** to maintain our efficiency floor.",
